  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Burning pain, numbness and tingling in the fingers of both hands, brought on by cold for many winters and worse this winter, with the fingers turning white then blue then red in the cold; average pain 6 of 10; cause not yet established at intake; nerve conduction studies and neurology consultation requested</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R20.2</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to his documented frostbite of the fingers; superseded by the diagnosis at the neurology consultation.</td>
